it-all and has a hot temper. Also we have other candidates facts. We can either support D or propose alternative. We need to be concise. Let's maybe support D but note concerns about cooperation and communication, and ask for more info from others about crew cooperation. Could also bring up candidate C's reliability and crew atmosphere. But we need to make a focused argument. Perhaps we can say we still recommend D but we need clarification on crew cooperation and communication. Or we could shift to Candidate C because of reliability and crew atmosphere. Let's see: Candidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So C has decision quality, calmness, technical competence, but communication issues and egocentric. D has problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogance and hot temper. Both have cooperation concerns. Which is stronger? D's strengths are more about reliability and problem solving, while C's strengths are decision speed and calmness. D's concerns are arrogance and hot temper, which may affect crew cooperation heavily. C's concerns are communication difficulty and egocentric, also affect cooperation. Both have issues. Might be better to ask for more info on crew cooperation for D. So we can keep provisional recommendation D, but ask for clarification. Provide evidence: D's strengths and concerns. So public message: I agree with Anna's recommendation for D, citing strengths, but highlight need to assess crew cooperation and communication. So vote D.\n\nProceed."}
