e B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Candidate C can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to bring new evidence not yet discussed: maybe candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness, but also communication tone. Or candidate C's excellent attention skills and concern for others. Could argue that candidate C's crew cooperation (puts concern for others above everything) may outweigh D's arrogance. Or we could ask for more info on D's crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Could keep D, but we might shift to C if we think crew cooperation is more critical. Let's evaluate: D's strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration, handling unexpected events. Concerns: arrogance, hot temper, moody, loner. C's strengths: quick correct decisions, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation), calm under pressure? Not explicitly but can make correct decisions quickly suggests decision quality. Concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Which is stronger? Crew cooperation is critical. D's interpersonal concerns may be severe. C's communication difficulty also severe. But C's concern for others suggests good teamwork. Might be better.\n\nThus we could argue that while D has strong technical and responsibility, his interpersonal issues may jeopardize crew cooperation, whereas C shows strong attention, decision quality, and a caring attitude toward others, making him a more balanced candidate. So we could shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: agree that D has strengths but highlight concerns. Provide evidence: D is regarded as a loner and moody (from our notes). C puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). Also C has excellent attention skills (attention). So we can argue C is better overall.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message: state we am less convinced by D due to interpersonal concerns, propose C as stronger overall, citing facts.\n\nProceed."}
